<title>SPAIN: TABLE-Repsol H1 attributable profit 61.63 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Repsol H1 attributable profit 61.63 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six months to end-June for Repsol group (in billions of pesetas, unless stated):  Net profit				71.20    vs    65.71</p>
<p> Minorities				 9.58    vs     4.26</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	     61.63    vs    61.45</p>
<p> Operating profit		     103.85    vs    96.05</p>
<p> Operating revenues		 1,519.48    vs 1,296.42</p>
<p> Financial losses			 9.23    vs     2.88</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit		   6.01    vs     0.63</p>
<p> Cash flow				152.13    vs   122.30</p>
<p> BALANCE TO DATE		     JUN 97	    DEC 96</p>
<p> Net fixed assets		   1,680.16    vs 1,486.81</p>
<p> Financial instruments		 15.00    vs    13.87</p>
<p> Liquid funds			   188.87    vs    87.08</p>
<p> Other current assets		 601.17    vs   570.81</p>
<p> Total current assets	     2,485.20    vs 2,158.57</p>
<p> Shareholder funds		    885.68    vs   847.85</p>
<p> Provisions			     114.52    vs   104.37</p>
<p> Minorities			     165.07    vs   139.04</p>
<p> Interest free debt		    92.92    vs    89.19</p>
<p> Medium/long term financial debt  384.42    vs   319.10</p>
<p> Short term financial debt	  316.22    vs   163.39</p>
<p> Other current liabilities	  526.36    vs   495.63</p>
<p> Total current liabilities	2,485.20    vs 2,158.57</p>
<p>NOTE: Repsol said in a statement net cash-flow levels were a clear reflection of the strength of results, showing the positive trend of the company's activities in the first half in Spain and Latin America.</p>
<p>Operating results rose despite the freeze in LPG prices.</p>
<p>Higher depreciation as a result of the asset restatement at the beginning of 1997 also cut into operating results.</p>
<p>Positive factors included a favourable trend in international refining margins and the appreciation of the dollar.</p>
<p>The company said investment carried out in the first half was 213.77 billion pesetas compared with 106.86 billion in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>Strong investment in Latin American continued, with acquisitions involving investments of 106 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom 34 1 585 2160</p>
